## Authentication
Bearer Token — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.

### Providing credentials
- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).
- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.

## Dependencies
- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.
- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).

## Endpoints

### Auth Flow (2)
- `GET /_next/static/{staticToken}/{staticToken}` — Retrieve static authentication tokens.
- `POST /sessions/{sessionId}` — Authenticate a user session.

### Data Read (3)
- `GET /attribution_trigger` — Get attribution trigger data.
- `GET /organizations/{organizationId}/routing` — Get routing information for an organization.
- `GET /v1/onelink` — Retrieve a OneLink URL.

### Data Write (3)
- `POST /{id}` — Write data to a resource.
- `POST /v1/{v1Id}` — Write data to a specific resource.
- `POST /wa/` — Write data to the workspace.

### Config (2)
- `GET /v1/config/{configHash}` — Retrieve a specific configuration.
- `GET /v2/recaptchaConfig` — Get reCAPTCHA configuration.

### Core API (1)
- `POST /api/v1/{v1Id}` — Call a core API endpoint.

## Quick Start

### OpenClaw (Unbrowse) workflow
- Authenticate in the browser first (no credentials are shipped with this skill).
- Capture fresh auth locally: run `unbrowse_capture` on an authenticated page for this domain.
- Execute via backend gate + client browser executor: `unbrowse_replay` with `executionMode="backend"`.

Example:
```text
unbrowse_replay { service: "replit", executionMode: "backend", endpoint: "GET /attribution_trigger" }
```

Here are a few examples to get you started with the Replit API. These examples assume you have a `client` object initialized with the necessary authentication and base URL.

```typescript
// Retrieve a specific configuration.  Useful for understanding server-side settings.
async function getConfig(configHash: string) {
  try {
    const config = await client.getConfig({ configHash });
    console.log("Configuration:", config);
    return config;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Error retrieving configuration:", error);
    return null;
  }
}
```

```typescript
// Call a core API endpoint.  This is a general-purpose endpoint, so you'll need to know the specific v1Id and payload.
async function callCoreApi(v1Id: string, payload: any) {
  try {
    const result = await client.api_v1({ v1Id, body: payload });
    console.log("Core API Result:", result);
    return result;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Error calling core API:", error);
    return null;
  }
}
